<title>UK: GKN shares lifted by helicopter deal.</title>
<headline>GKN shares lifted by helicopter deal.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in UK engineering and automotive components group GKN Plc jumped on Monday following news the company won a contract worth 100 million stg to sell the German government seven Super Lynx helicopters.</p>
<p>GKN shares touched an intraday high of 1,115p on the news but slipped back to trade at 1,112-1/2p by 1105 GMT, up 12p on the day with 183,000 shares traded. The overall market was weak.</p>
<p>&quot;It's not the biggest deal but, given the lack of other news in the market and relatively low volumes, it has given the stock a lift,&quot; one marketmaker said.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
